gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.tooltip=Machine Type: §eRemote Multiblock Host§r\nRuns explicitly bound machines of one type from centralized I/O and power hatches\nConsumers use central energy hatches; generators use a central dynamo hatch\nSupports turbine, naquadah, gas and liquid-fuel multiblock generators while retaining rotor, fuel, coolant, warm-up, efficiency and pollution mechanics\nRemote machines remain formed and keep their original power hatches to define per-machine rating and mechanics\nBatch mode is supported; disabling work finishes current jobs; progress is shown in seconds\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\n§eBinding setup:\n§f1. Craft and hold a Hosted Machine Binder\n§f2. Shift-left-click the host controller to record it\n§f3. Right-click a remote controller to add or remove it\n§f4. Drone DownLinks only provide maintenance and never auto-host machines\n§7§m-----------------------------------------\nHold §l[LSHIFT]§r§7 to display structure guidance
gt.blockmachines.matterblueprints.multimachine.host.tooltip_secondary=§fSize: §69§7x§67§7x§66§7 (§6L§7x§6W§7x§6H§7) §c(Open machine room and roof)\n§fStructure:\n   §fController: §7Front center of the lower wall\n   §663 §fSuperplasticizer-Treated High Strength Concrete: §7Complete bottom layer\n   §632+ §fHosted Machine-Room Casings: §7Replaceable positions across three wall levels\n   §613 §fFixed casings and §636 §fFlowing Data-Light Casings\n   §61 §fDrone Receiver Core: §7Roof center\n   §eExactly 1 §fMaintenance Hatch (Drone DownLink allowed): §7Any replaceable position\n   §eConsumer hosting: §fnormal, multi-amp or laser Energy Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n   §eGenerator hosting: §fnormal Dynamo or Laser Source Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n   §e1+ §fInput Bus or Input Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n   §e1+ §fOutput Bus or Output Hatch: §7Any replaceable position\n§7§m------------------------------\n§fUse the Multiblock Structure §9Hologram §1Projector§f on the controller to visualize/build it!
